# Breakout Economy — Policy Flight Simulator (SPEC v0.1)

## 1) What we are building (Overview)
We are building an interactive “Policy Flight Simulator” that lets users explore a fiscally-solvent Universal Basic Income (UBI) model funded by a Token Tax on electronic value flow, plus a simplified income tax structure and captured welfare efficiency savings. Users adjust key policy parameters with sliders and immediately see the impact on total revenue, total obligations, surplus/deficit, and example “persona” outcomes across income brackets. The system is educational and exploratory: it makes the mechanics transparent, interactive, and testable—without storing personal data or providing financial advice.

---

## 2) Primary goals (Product outcomes)
- Make UBI + Token Tax mechanics understandable through real-time simulation.
- Demonstrate how “incentive slopes” avoid welfare cliffs (work is always rewarded).
- Provide transparent fiscal solvency outputs (surplus/deficit) with clear assumptions.
- Provide a simple v1 interface that is engaging, fast, and deterministic.

---

## 3) What is in scope (v0.1 – v1.0)
### In scope
- A deterministic math engine (source of truth) that computes:
  - Token Tax revenue from “Flow Base” and “Tax Rate”
  - Income tax revenue from tier rules
  - Welfare savings credit
  - UBI obligations and total obligations
  - Net surplus/deficit
  - Citizen supplement curve (Apex + Glide + Breakout point)
  - Persona comparison outputs for multiple earned-income levels
- A UI with sliders and immediate feedback (red/green solvency indicator)
- Basic charts/tables (by v0.3)
- Educational tooltips / glossary (by v0.4)
- Optional crowdsourcing module (submit configurations + leaderboard) (v1.0)

### Out of scope (for now)
- Predictive macroeconomic modeling (inflation, GDP feedback loops)
- Financial advice, tax filing guidance, or user-specific recommendations
- Storing user PII or linking configurations to identities
- Real payments, real token taxation, or integration with government systems

---

## 4) Non-functional requirements (Engineering constraints)
- Deterministic: same inputs always produce same outputs.
- Fast: UI updates in < 500ms for recalculation.
- Transparent: formulas visible in-app (at least in a “How it works” section).
- No PII required. Anonymous analytics/config submissions only (optional).
- Clear disclaimers: educational simulation only.

---

## 5) Core model assumptions (Defaults; adjustable where noted)
### Constants (default)
- Adult population: 265,000,000
- Annual electronic flow base: 1,000,000,000,000,000 (1 Quadrillion)
- Welfare savings credit: 630,000,000,000 (630B)
- Government operating requirement: 2,740,000,000,000 (2.74T)
- Base UBI per adult (annual): 12,000

### Default policy parameters (user adjustable)
- Token tax rate: 0.35% (0.0035)
- Breakout point (income threshold): 60,000
- Tier 1 bracket: 60,001–135,000 at 19% marginal
- Tier 2 bracket: >135,000 at 29% marginal
- Supplement curve:
  - Apex earned income point: 24,000
  - Bonus at apex: 6,000
  - Glide taper ends at breakout point: 60,000
  - Taper slope: -0.16 (meaning: benefits reduce by $0.16 per $1 earned between apex and breakout)

Note: The supplement curve should ensure "no cliffs" and never reduce net income as earned income rises.

---

## 6) Inputs and outputs (API contract for the math engine)
### Inputs (PolicyConfig)
- tokenTaxRate (0.001–0.01 allowed)
- flowBaseAnnual (default 1e15; optional slider in later version)
- ubiAnnualPerAdult (0–20000 allowed)
- adultPopulation (default 265e6; constant for v0.x)
- welfareSavingsCredit (default 630e9)
- govtOperatingRequirement (default 2.74e12)
- breakoutPoint (30000–80000 allowed)
- tier1Rate (default 0.19)
- tier2Rate (default 0.29)
- tier1Start (default breakoutPoint)
- tier2Start (default 135000)
- supplementApexIncome (default 24000)
- supplementApexBonus (default 6000)
- supplementGlideSlope (default -0.16)

### Outputs (SimulationResult)
- revenue:
  - tokenTaxRevenue
  - incomeTaxRevenue (if modeled; may be simplified in v0.1)
  - welfareSavingsCredit
  - totalRevenue
- obligations:
  - ubiCost
  - govtOperatingRequirement
  - totalObligations
- balance:
  - surplusDeficit (totalRevenue - totalObligations)
  - isSolvent (boolean)
- citizenModel:
  - supplementFunctionSummary (human readable)
  - personaOutcomes[]:
    - label (Starter/Professional/Manager/Executive)
    - earnedIncome
    - ubi
    - supplement
    - incomeTax
    - netIncome (earnedIncome + ubi + supplement - incomeTax)
- diagnostics:
  - warnings[] (e.g., “Token tax rate unusually high—may imply capital flight risk” as informational only)

---

## 7) Supplement curve (definition)
We will implement a “Floor & Launchpad” supplement that:
- Gives everyone base UBI.
- Adds a bonus/supplement that peaks at earned income = 24,000 (Apex).
- Tapers down smoothly until earned income = Breakout Point.
- Never creates a cliff (no sudden drops).
- Never makes net income decrease with higher earnings.

Reference behavior:
- At earned income 24,000: supplement = 6,000
- At earned income 60,000: supplement = 0

